vealed_anchor_rearm","kind":"invariant","state":"verified_current","summary":"Automatic repricing or manual Rehide of a zero-fill REVEALED placement persists one placement-scoped cancel intent and remains REVEALED until matching authenticated terminal truth. A matching zero-fill cancellation restores that placement quantity to HIDDEN at the desired canonical price; the existing reveal policy owns re-entry, and only this completed REVEALED-to-HIDDEN transition resets the time-delay arm point. Parent projection atomically records the placement cancellation and logical PENDING state only when durable execution-owner guards pass. Manual Rehide uses the configured price and preserves condition configuration and repricing metrics.","tags":["stealth","reprice","rearm","cancellation","reveal","rehide"]}
